From 16b6cf37e5aaa046df86269ec245a12eaeb762ca Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 28 Nov 2026 02:14:30 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] sim/rt/device: only visible events synchronize; one-retry
 crossings

After each saved boundary the engine runs on with its inputs held (`look`,
at most `look_cap` = 1024 event ticks) to the first tick an output pin's
level or drive changes or the engine stops; `pendingBreakpoint` reports
that time (merged with any further visible change less than `ttol` after
it), not the next internal event, and a step that reaches neither it nor an
input crossing runs no engine. `wakes` is the union over the ticks `look`
ran; a crossing past them wakes conservatively.

A crossing more than `ttol` late in a step that wakes a process now
returns `.request_reject_at` (its secant time + ttol/2), so a host re-lands
once; `late_cross` stays for hosts that query.

A `profile` debug flag prints each active step's cost split.

tests/host/vdev_host.zig: v_edge_clock (metamorphic with v_edge), the
retry, and v_skew's merge window, each red on 0bc0092; `test-vdev` runs
the host alone.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_014DSyq6YHPYv8k8qvURepx5
