From b31d568e5803254f1802fc8d45cafb94d2de1ece Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 28 Nov 2026 02:14:30 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] sim/rt/State: a quiet state allocates no stdout buffer

`quietState` built the 64 KiB stdout buffer a quiet engine never writes, so
the contract device's per-step arena outgrew the allocator's size classes
and mapped fresh pages on every active step. `initTo` now prints into the
quiet sink from the start and allocates the buffer only for a real run.
On a 2000-flip-flop design (ESpice, Debug): arena 105912 -> 9358 bytes per
active step, (rebuild + restore + save) / run 3.93 -> 1.30.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_014DSyq6YHPYv8k8qvURepx5
